  ("Subtracting a negative number is the same as adding, so a negative discrepancy makes the subtraction **move x upward**.", "Subtracting a negative number is the same as adding. So a negative discrepancy makes the subtraction **move x upward**."),
  ("The value 98 appears twice in the list, and since each draw is random, the same value can be picked more than once.", "The value 98 appears twice in the list. Each draw is random, so the same value can be picked more than once."),
  ("Individual steps can move away from the true average, as happened when 98 was drawn, but over many updates the random pushes up and down balance out and the estimate settles near 80.", "Individual steps can move away from the true average, as happened when 98 was drawn. Over many updates, though, the random pushes up and down balance out, and the estimate settles near 80."),
  ("Each random observation is sometimes above and sometimes below the average, so on average the estimate is pulled toward the mean of the data, 80.", "Each random observation is sometimes above and sometimes below the average. So on average the estimate is pulled toward the mean of the data, 80."),
